From 2eeb9d4239c1a8d59e403f00a2c27399a3e12d06 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dominggoes Isakh <drjisakh@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:22:06 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] SurfaceFlinger: Disable SF HWC backpressure

Gate wouldBackpressureHwc() behind persist.sys.enable_sf_hwc_backpressure
(default true, so stock behavior is unchanged unless overridden) -
lets legacy-kernel/HWC devices disable HWC backpressure handling at
runtime instead of relying on it unconditionally.

Adapted for LineageOS 24.0: pacesetterFrameTarget was renamed to a
pointer, pacesetterFrameTargetPtr, since the original 23.2-era patch.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I30bc9c4c0c45b952a81f82156002d619825d27ba
---
 services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp b/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
index 9128394aa1..cf2e5107b9 100644
--- a/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
+++ b/services/surfaceflinger/SurfaceFlinger.cpp
@@ -3066,7 +3066,8 @@ bool SurfaceFlinger::commit(PhysicalDisplayId pacesetterId,
         }
     }
 
-    if (pacesetterFrameTargetPtr->wouldBackpressureHwc()) {
+    if (base::GetBoolProperty("persist.sys.enable_sf_hwc_backpressure"s, true)
+            && pacesetterFrameTargetPtr->wouldBackpressureHwc()) {
         if (mBackpressureGpuComposition || pacesetterFrameTargetPtr->didMissHwcFrame()) {
             mScheduler->getVsyncSchedule()->getTracker().onFrameMissed(
                     pacesetterFrameTargetPtr->expectedPresentTime());
-- 
